/**
 * Platform Owner PO-03A (primary-owner protection and read-only user-seat accounting — development only) — the approved
 * change to files the DEV-UI-01.7, ACC-01, LCP, PO-01A, PO-01B, PO-01B.1, PO-02A, PO-02B, PO-02C, PO-02C.1, PO-02D1A,
 * PO-02D1A.1, PO-02D1B, PO-02D2 and PO-02D3 verifiers freeze.
 *
 * PO-03A changes five customer files, each narrowly. The Team tab's two member actions (src/app/(app)/settings/team/
 * actions.ts — changeRoleAction and toggleMemberActiveAction keep their signatures, their requireRole("owner", "admin")
 * gate and their revalidation, and now delegate to the Team-change service, which runs the existing checks again on
 * rows locked in one READ COMMITTED transaction — organization row, then the actor's and target's user rows by id,
 * then the primary-owner mapping — and refuses to demote or deactivate the company's mapped primary owner; the
 * add-member action is unchanged). The Team panel (team-panel.tsx — a display-only seat card, a "Primary owner" badge,
 * and a menu that offers the primary owner no other role and no deactivation; the server refuses either way). The
 * Business Settings page that hosts it (organization/page.tsx — reads the session's own company's ownership summary).
 * The activity writer (src/lib/activity.ts — logActivity takes an optional transaction executor, default db, so the
 * Team change and its activity row commit together; every existing caller is unchanged). The shared dictionary
 * (src/lib/i18n/dict.ts — the new strings in Arabic, appended). It changes three platform files, all display-only: the
 * console company detail (companies/[orgId]/page.tsx — a Users & seats panel), its strings (components/platform/
 * i18n.ts) and the companies read model (lib/platform/companies.ts — counts, the subscription's seat snapshot and the
 * primary-owner designation, fail-soft). And it changes the two freeze verifiers (this layer's hooks). It adds six
 * files: the read-only primary-owner and seat-accounting cores (src/lib/platform/), the Team ownership gate (the ONE
 * customer module that reaches those cores, fail-closed when the foundation is expected and missing), the Team-change
 * service, the summary types and the seat card. No schema module, SQL, migration, seed, session, sign-in,
 * registration, MFA, business or acceptance file is in either list; seat limits are not enforced.
 *
 * The rule for an approved change is the one C8, ACC-01, the LCP stage and PO-01A…PO-02D3 used: no re-baseline. Each
 * changed file's hunks are recorded here byte for byte, [1d036d6's text, PO-03A's text]; undone, the file is PO-02D3's
 * (1d036d6) to the byte (PO03A_BASE_SHA), so every older pin keeps its strength. Each freeze verifier's PO-03A check
 * proves the hunks are each file's only change and the added files are exactly as recorded.
 *
 * Generated from the diff against PO03A_BASE (each hunk widened with context until it is unique in both files, its
 * 1d036d6 form nowhere in PO-03A's); changing a PO-03A file means regenerating this record, which is then part of the
 * change under review.
 */
